*****in java OOP basically focus on data and becauze of that its uses pass by value rather than pass by reference to maintain the consistency


types of object creation: 

shallow copy : copies each values of one object to other object as a reference so that any change made by the one object 2 is made to object 1 as well
Stud a = new Stud();
stud b = a

deep copy: copies each values of one object to other object so that any change made by the one object 2 is not made to object 1 to maintain the consistancy 
Stud a = new Stud();
stud b.set(a.get)

