string constatnt pool or why string is immutable - when object of string is created then its stored in string constatnt pool and all strings are belongs to a string constant pool and it does not allow the creation of duplicate string and hence its immutable to avoid repeatation
String s = "ss"
String a = "ss"
here both string have same value so in string constatnt pool it refers to single location in string constatnt pool area so avoid extra memory utilization

String str1 = new String("bbah") - creates the 2 objects , one is in heap memory and 1 is in string constatnt pool

